    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d34">

                <pb facs="0151" n="57" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg57"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-08-20"><hi rendition="#italic">August 20, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received Sept. 28.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2579.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In acknowledgment of your dispatch No.
                    1301, of the 13th ultimo, I have the honor to state that the claim referred to
                    as still pending, in the Chinese minister’s note of the 8th July, copy of which
                    is inclosed in the above dispatch, is the claim of the American Baptist
                    Missionary Union, payment of which has heretofore been reported to the
                    Department.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
